IMPORT prelude

-- Road Traffic Act 1961 (Singapore) -- forfeiture of the vehicle after dangerous or careless driving (s 65AA), and the
-- driver's duties after an accident (s 84).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Road Traffic Act 1961 -- forfeiture and accidents`

§§ `65AA -- forfeiture of the vehicle`

-- s 65AA(1): where a person is convicted of dangerous or careless driving causing DEATH or GRIEVOUS HURT as a SERIOUS or
-- SERIOUS REPEAT offender (ss 64(2), (3), 65(2), (3) with (c) or (d)), and a motor vehicle was used, the court "is to, on
-- the application of the Public Prosecutor, make an order for the forfeiture of the motor vehicle, UNLESS the court is
-- satisfied that -- (c) the person who has committed the offence is NOT THE OWNER of the motor vehicle; AND (d) ... had used
-- the motor vehicle WITHOUT THE CONSENT of the owner".
-- (2): where a person is convicted of dangerous driving causing DEATH as a first or repeat offender (s 64(6)(a), (b)), "or
-- section 26(2) of the Police Force Act 2004 (which offence is committed on or after 1 November 2019)", forfeiture
-- follows unless the same two conditions are met "or (b) the court has other good reasons for ordering otherwise".
--
-- Under (1), lending your car is consent: a drunk friend who kills with it costs you the car, and the court has no
-- residual discretion. Under (2) it has one.
--
-- AND (2) CITES A PROVISION THAT IS NOT AN OFFENCE. In the Police Force Act 2004 as deposited in this repository
-- (see subjects/sg/police-force-act-2004), s 26(2) is the power of a police officer to ORDER a driver to stop at a barrier;
-- the offence of failing to stop is s 26(5), with the penalty in s 26(8). Those subsections were rearranged by Act 21 of
-- 2021 with effect from 1 January 2022. Read literally, no one can be "convicted of an offence under ... section 26(2)"
-- of the Police Force Act as it now stands.
DECLARE ForfeitureCase HAS
    `harm` IS A STRING
    `is a serious or serious repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dangerous rather than careless` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offender is not the owner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `used without the owner's consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court has other good reasons` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the case` IS A ForfeitureCase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsection (1) applies` IF
        `the case`'s `is a serious or serious repeat offender`
    AND (`the case`'s `harm` EQUALS "death" OR `the case`'s `harm` EQUALS "grievous hurt")

GIVEN `the case` IS A ForfeitureCase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsection (2) applies` IF
        NOT `the case`'s `is a serious or serious repeat offender`
    AND `the case`'s `dangerous rather than careless`
    AND `the case`'s `harm` EQUALS "death"

GIVEN `the case` IS A ForfeitureCase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner's escape applies` IF
    `the case`'s `the offender is not the owner` AND `the case`'s `used without the owner's consent`

GIVEN `the case` IS A ForfeitureCase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vehicle must be forfeited` IF
        (    `subsection (1) applies` `the case`
         AND NOT `the owner's escape applies` `the case`)
    OR  (    `subsection (2) applies` `the case`
         AND NOT `the owner's escape applies` `the case`
         AND NOT `the case`'s `the court has other good reasons`)

DECLARE PFASubsection IS ONE OF
    `section 26(2), the power to order a driver to stop`
    `section 26(5), the offence of failing to stop`

GIVEN `the subsection` IS A PFASubsection
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a person can be convicted of an offence under the cited subsection` IF
    CONSIDER `the subsection`
    WHEN `section 26(5), the offence of failing to stop` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 65AA(4): a seized vehicle "must be released at the end of one month" if there is no prosecution.
GIVEN `days since seizure` IS A NUMBER, `prosecuted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seized vehicle must be released` IF
    (NOT `prosecuted`) AND `days since seizure` GREATER THAN 30

§§ `84 -- after an accident`

-- s 84(1): where an accident owing to the presence of a motor vehicle on a road results in damage or injury, the driver
-- "must stop" and (a) give particulars to anyone at the scene with reasonable grounds to ask, or (b) if no one is there,
-- take reasonable steps to inform the owner of the damaged vehicle or structure.
-- (2): report to the police "as soon as reasonably practicable within 24 HOURS" UNLESS (a) particulars were given to a
-- person at the scene, or (b) the owner has contacted the driver.
-- (2A), (2B): for an animal, stop if the driver has reasonable grounds to believe it has an owner or is a hazard; give
-- particulars; warn other road users and tell the police of a hazard.
-- (3): render assistance reasonably required.
-- (4): where someone is killed or seriously injured or there is serious damage, no one may move the vehicles except to
-- extricate people, prevent fire or obstruction.
--
-- A driver who scrapes a parked car with no one about, leaves a note and is contacted by the owner, need not report to the
-- police; one who leaves a note and is not contacted must report within 24 hours.
DECLARE Accident HAS
    `damage or injury resulted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `stopped` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gave particulars to a person at the scene` IS A BOOLEAN
    `someone with reasonable grounds was at the scene` IS A BOOLEAN
    `took reasonable steps to inform the owner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner contacted the driver` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reported to the police within 24 hours` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the accident` IS AN Accident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the driver met the duty at the scene` IF
        NOT `the accident`'s `damage or injury resulted`
    OR  (    `the accident`'s `stopped`
         AND (IF `the accident`'s `someone with reasonable grounds was at the scene`
              THEN `the accident`'s `gave particulars to a person at the scene`
              ELSE `the accident`'s `took reasonable steps to inform the owner`))

GIVEN `the accident` IS AN Accident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the driver must report to the police` IF
        `the accident`'s `damage or injury resulted`
    AND NOT `the accident`'s `gave particulars to a person at the scene`
    AND NOT `the accident`'s `the owner contacted the driver`

GIVEN `the accident` IS AN Accident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the driver is in breach of section 84` IF
        NOT `the driver met the duty at the scene` `the accident`
    OR  (    `the driver must report to the police` `the accident`
         AND NOT `the accident`'s `reported to the police within 24 hours`)

-- Animals: stop if the driver reasonably believes it has an owner or is a hazard.
GIVEN `reasonably believes the animal has an owner` IS A BOOLEAN, `reasonably believes it is a hazard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the driver must stop for the animal` IF
    `reasonably believes the animal has an owner` OR `reasonably believes it is a hazard`
